 "equipment_type": "Power meter",
 "applies_to": "T203PM100-MU / T203PM300-MU / T203PM600-MU per user manual MI00571-3-EN.",
 "summary": "The T203PM is a DIN-rail transducer that measures true-RMS AC or DC voltage and current on one phase and works out power, energy, power factor, frequency and THD. It answers Modbus RTU on RS-485 (and on USB for setup). This map covers the float measurement block, min/max values, scaled integer copies, the 64-bit energy counters, the command register and the analog/digital output setup.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": null,
  "parity": null,
  "data_bits": null,
  "stop_bits": null,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "Modicon",
  "note": "The table prints both the 4x number (40002) and the 0-based offset (1). The offset is the wire address: 40002 is sent as 1."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "T203PM100-MU / T203PM300-MU / T203PM600-MU User Manual",
  "doc_number": "MI00571-3-EN",
  "revision_date": "2023-03-16",
  "url": "https://www.seneca.it/media/6849089/mi00571-3-en.pdf",
  "pages": "Modbus rules pp. 16-21; register table pp. 22-27"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Only function codes 03, 06 and 16 are supported; every value, including measurements, is a holding register.",
  "32-bit values are MSW in the lower register (ABCD) and 64-bit counters are MMSW first (ABCD). The manual says adding 1000 to an address gives the same 32-bit value word-swapped (e.g. current at 41107); that mirror block is not listed here.",
  "Integer copies are scaled as printed: V/10, A/10, W/10, Hz/10, PF/1000, THD/10; energy counters are Wh/10 (varh/10, VAh/10).",
  "The table marks the command register (40005) RO, but the manual's procedures write commands to it, so it is listed as RW.",
  "Registers marked RW* are stored in flash and survive about 10,000 writes.",
  "Left out: reserved registers and the integer min/max copies (40197-40218); the float min/max block covers the same values.",
  "The manual does not state factory defaults for address, baud rate or parity."
 ],
